  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Farlowella platorynchus Retzer &amp; Page, 1997</li><li>Common names: Broadsnout Twig Catfish</li><li>Size: 194 mm (7.6\") SL</li><li>Temperature: 22.0-27.0°C</li><li>Habitat: Blackwater</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<p>South America: Upper and lower Amazon River basin, including the Upper Amazon, Marañón and Ucayali. Type locality: Yarinachocha, Río Ucayali drainage, Ucayali Dept., Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<p>Suggested tankmates: Tetras or Rasboras are best. Avoid fast or \"nippy\" fishes such as Danios or Barbs. Will do well with Corydoras catfish, but larger catfish or cichlids are to be avoided.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: Unreported.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<p>Identification: The genus Farlowella is distinguished by its elongate and slender body with a pronounced rostrum (of variable length), having the dorsal fin located near the middle of the body and only slightly anterior to the anal fin, and having a brownish color with two lateral dark stripes beginning at the tip of the rostrum, passing through the eyes and ending at the tail.</p><p>Etymology: The genus is named after W. G. Farlow, from Harvard University. The specific epithet refers to its broad (platys = broad) snout (rhynchos = snout).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1190",
      "html": "<p>Proc. Acad. Nat. Sci. Phila. v. 147 71 Fig. 44</p>"
    }
  ],
